# Trivy suppressions. Each entry needs a one-line reason — audit before
# adding to this file. Mirrors the same trade-off discipline as
# `.checkov.yaml`.

# Geo-redundant replication: LRS chosen for cost (see CKV_AZURE_206 in
# .checkov.yaml for the same trade-off).
AZU-0058

# Storage Analytics logging is deferred. Same as CKV_AZURE_33 — proper
# fix is Diagnostic Settings to a Log Analytics workspace, which is its
# own commit.
AZU-0057

# Infrastructure encryption (double encryption at rest). Closing this
# requires destroying and recreating the storage account, which would
# break the SP's manually-granted Storage Blob Data Contributor role
# assignment. Deferred to the "SA modernization" commit that handles
# AZU-0012 (service-tag restriction) at the same time, where we can
# coordinate the RBAC re-grant cleanly.
AZU-0061

# Default network action deny + restricted origin. Microsoft.Cdn/profiles
# (Front Door, any SKU) is NOT in the supported resource type list for
# storage account resource instance rules — see
# https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-network-security-trusted-azure-services
# — so there is no way to deny by default and allow Standard FD as an
# exception. Only paths to compliance are:
#   - Upgrade to FD Premium and use actual Private Link to origin
#     (~£200/mo uplift), or
#   - Replace the storage origin with a service in the supported list.
# Deliberately accepted as a known trade-off of the Standard SKU.
AZU-0012

# Data Factory public access disabled. Mirror of Checkov CKV_AZURE_104
# — fixing requires Managed VNet IR + private endpoints, ~£20+/mo. ADF
# stays public for the IaC-pattern demo. Productionisation path
# documented in /docs/architecture/data-platform-hld.
AZU-0035

